# BQ quests [pack=gtit] BEGIN
### Quest Lines ###

## GT Interesting Thing

betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Interesting Thing
betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=§3§lFeature overview§r%nThis GTIT quest line covers the vending machine, gifts, sign-in, lottery, mail and team wallets, together with coins, float cores, scanning, rings, infinite storage, reincarnation and the dimension pocket.%n%n§3§lQuest route§r%nThere are §135§r quest entries. The eastern branch introduces operations, the western branch introduces tools, and the line extends to quest-gated trades. Complete information quests using their checkboxes and item quests according to their retrieval or crafting requirements.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lTwo Faces of the Cat Economy
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=§3§lPurpose and mechanics§r%nGTIT provides two groups of features: the vending machine, starter gift, sign-in, lottery and mail form its operations system; coins, float cores, infinite storage and rings form its personal tool system. There are §18§r rings: §17§r functional rings and Windrider, crafted from those seven.%n%n§3§lQuest route§r%nThe eastern branch covers operations, and the western branch covers tools. Read this introduction, then tick the checkbox to complete the quest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§6§lThe Cat Ops Deck
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=§3§lStarter gift and configuration§r%nEach player automatically receives a §2Starter Gift§r on their first login. A claim record prevents duplicate grants. An administrator can reset that record to issue another gift on the player's next login.%n%nGift contents, trade entries, sign-in rewards and lottery pools each have their own configuration. Administrators can also edit vending-machine trade entries in its GUI.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Starter Gift for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Alternatively, tick the checkbox. Either task completes this quest, so players who have already opened or no longer have their gift can use the checkbox.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§2§lUnboxing the Cat's Welcome Kit
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=§3§lDefault gift§r%nThe default guaranteed contents are bread ×§116§r, torches ×§164§r, a bed ×§11§r, chests ×§18§r and a Neko Coin ×§11§r, plus §12§r random rings from Skywalk, Ironheart, Dragon's Breath, Mountainbreaker and Tempest. Servers can change these contents.%n%n§3§lAdministrator configuration§r%n/gtit gift certain sets the current inventory as the guaranteed list; /gtit gift random <count> sets the random pool; /gtit gift reset restores defaults. /gtit gift claimlist lists claim records, and /gtit gift claimreset <all|player> resets records so the affected players receive another gift on their next login.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold a bed ×§11§r and torches ×§164§r for retrieval. §2Neither is consumed.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§6§lBuild the Cat Machine
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=§3§lVending-machine functions§r%nThe Neko Vending Machine provides trade, sign-in, lottery and mail interfaces. It has §18§r input inventory slots and §1100§r output inventory slots. Trades check available output space.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nObtain §11§r vending-machine controller and hold it in your inventory for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Placing the machine in the world does not replace this inventory check.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§d§lWiring the Cat into ME
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=§3§lConnecting to ME§r%nAn ME Uplink Hatch can replace any casing block on the vending machine. Each machine accepts at most §11§r hatch.%n%nWith a valid, active AE network connection, the machine can extract materials from ME. To send output into ME, also enable ME output mode in the machine GUI.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r ME Uplink Hatch for retrieval. It is §2not consumed§r and can be installed afterward.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§6§lWallets, Import and Teams
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=§3§lWallet and physical coins§r%nPlace coins in an input slot and use import to turn them into wallet balance. Export converts balance back into physical coins. With a valid ME connection, coins can also be imported from or exported to the network.%n%n§3§lPersonal and team wallets§r%nPlayers without a team use their personal wallet. Joining a team automatically switches access to its shared wallet. Personal balances remain separate and become accessible again after leaving; joining does not transfer them into the team wallet.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nView the wallet interface and understand import, export and sharing, then tick the checkbox.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§2§lDaily Sign-In
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=§3§lDaily and milestone rewards§r%nClaim daily rewards from the calendar in the sign-in tab. Defaults are §110§r Neko Coins on weekdays, §120§r on weekends and a streak coefficient of §11.0§r; servers can adjust these values.%n%nEach streak milestone can be claimed once per month. Cumulative milestones are one-time account rewards: the default §130 / 100 / 365§r days award §1100 / 300 / 1000§r coins respectively.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the sign-in and milestone rules, then tick the checkbox. This quest does not check an actual sign-in record.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§8§lPaid to Idle
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=§3§lOnline-time rewards§r%nDefault daily tiers award §15§r coins after §130 minutes§r online, §120§r after §12 hours§r and §150§r after §15 hours§r. Servers can adjust the tiers and rewards.%n%nTime accrues only while the player is online. Tiers reset daily, and each tier can be claimed once per day.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the timing and claiming rules, then tick the checkbox. This quest does not require proof of online time.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§d§lThe Roulette and Its Pity
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=§3§lDraw costs§r%nBy default, each Neko-pool draw costs §15§r Neko Coins, and each Shimmering-pool draw costs §11§r Shimmering Neko Coin. Servers can adjust pool costs and pity settings.%n%n§3§lPity rules§r%nDefault soft pity begins after §130§r consecutive misses of high-rarity rewards. Each additional miss increases the high-rarity entry weight multiplier by §15%§r; §cthis is not a percentage-point increase in drop chance§r. Default hard pity guarantees EPIC or better at §150§r draws in the Neko pool and §130§r in the Shimmering pool. Counters are shared within each team, separately for each pool.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the cost and pity rules, then tick the checkbox. This quest charges no draw fee and does not require a draw.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§6§lSaving for a Ten-Pull
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=§3§lTen-pulls and delivery§r%nDefault animations last §12.8 seconds§r for a single draw and §11.4 seconds§r for a ten-pull. The server waits another §1150 milliseconds§r after the animation before delivering rewards.%n%nMembers of the same team share pity counters within each pool. Any member's draws advance that pool's counter. A ten-pull still requires payment for its draws.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the ten-pull cost and shared-pity rules, then tick the checkbox. This quest does not require holding funds or performing a ten-pull.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§3§lThe Cat Post Office
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=§3§lMailbox and attachments§r%nUse the Mail tab to view your mailbox. Each player can store up to §150§r mails, with up to §15§r item stacks attached to each. Mail for an offline recipient remains in their mailbox to view and claim after logging in.%n%n§3§lDeletion and completion§r%n§cMail with unclaimed attachments cannot be deleted.§r Claim its attachments first. Read the mailbox instructions, then tick the checkbox.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§2§lBirthdays, Festivals, Cake
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=§3§lBirthdays and anniversaries§r%nSet your birthday in the sign-in tab using MM-dd, and add up to §15§r custom anniversaries. Administrators maintain festival and blessing templates. The default birthday mail includes a §2cake§r.%n%n§3§lLunar festivals and solar terms§r%nLunar festivals are converted automatically to that year's dates; §clunar leap months do not trigger them§r. The system also sends mail for §111§r key solar terms, with seasonal crop attachments. Servers can configure the contents.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the blessing-mail and date-setting instructions, then tick the checkbox. Setting a birthday or receiving mail is not required.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§c§lServer Ops Appendix
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=§3§lOptional administration notes§r%nThis quest is for server administrators and is not a prerequisite for other quests. Gifts, trades, sign-in and lottery each have configuration files under config/gtit.%n%n§3§lTrade editing and reload§r%nUse /gtit nekovm edit on|off to switch trade editing mode and modify entries in the vending-machine GUI. After saving the configuration, use /gtit nekovm reload to reload it.%n%n§3§lQuest gating and completion§r%nGate IDs accept high:low, UUID, standard Base64 and URL-safe Base64; padding is optional for the last form. §cGates allow access if BetterQuesting is absent or its query fails.§r Administrators should verify the configuration and dependencies. Read these notes, then tick the checkbox.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lThe Player's Toolbox
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=§3§lCoin sources§r%nOrdinary Neko Coins are included in §17§r structure-chest loot tables, with §12–8§r coins per loot entry and a stack limit of §164§r. Shimmering Coins are not registered in those chest tables; sources include fishing, exchange trades and quest rewards.%n%n§3§lFishing chances§r%nEach successful catch first rolls the default §12%§r chance for a Shimmering Coin. If that misses, it rolls the default §110%§r chance for an ordinary coin. The resulting default ordinary-coin chance is §19.8%§r. Servers can adjust both chances.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §18§r ordinary Neko Coins for retrieval. They are §2not consumed§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§6§lSixty-Four to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=§3§lForward exchange§r%nThe bundled vending-machine trades include an exchange of §164§r Neko Coins for §11§r Shimmering Coin. By default, each player must wait §122 hours§r after using this entry before using it again. Server settings determine the actual price and cooldown.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Shimmering Coin for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. The coin does not have to come from this particular exchange.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§6§lThe Fifty-Six Spread
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=§3§lReverse exchange and spread§r%nAnother bundled entry exchanges §11§r Shimmering Coin for §156§r Neko Coins, with a default per-player cooldown of §122 hours§r. Its cooldown is separate from the forward exchange.%n%nAt the default prices, exchanging §164§r Neko Coins forward and then back returns §156§r coins, a difference of §18§r. This is the spread between two entries; §ca round trip reduces your coin holdings§r.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the spread and independent-cooldown rules, then tick the checkbox. No exchange is required.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§2§lTake Flight on Steak
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=§3§lFood-powered flight§r%nEquip a Float Core in a universal Baubles accessory slot. With a food level of at least §16§r, it grants §2creative flight§r. Flying adds §10.02§r exhaustion per tick, affecting saturation before food level; it does not directly subtract that many hunger points.%n%n§3§lFlight limit and completion§r%n§cFlight is disabled below food level §16§r§c. Bring food and watch for a safe landing.§r Craft §11§r Float Core to complete this quest. Holding an existing core does not replace the crafting check.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§6§lFuel for Flight
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=§3§lFlight supplies§r%nThe basic Float Core uses food reserves through exhaustion. Cooked beef restores food level and is also one of its crafting ingredients. Bring food before flying and replenish it as you approach the flight cutoff.%n%n§3§lSubmission and reward§r%nSubmit cooked beef ×§116§r to complete the quest; §cthe beef is consumed§r. The quest separately awards Delighted Meals ×§18§r as additional supplies, rather than returning the beef.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§6§lThirty-Two Million EU Wings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=§3§lElectric flight§r%nThe Electric Float Core stores up to §132,000,000 EU§r and accepts charging at up to LV's §132 EU/t§r. While equipped, flight consumes §1128 EU/t§r.%n%n§3§lLow power and completion§r%nIf power is insufficient, a food level of at least §16§r allows flight using §10.01§r exhaustion per tick instead. §cFlight cannot continue when both power and food are insufficient.§r Craft §11§r Electric Float Core to complete the quest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§3§lThe Mind's Eye
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=§3§lScan range and modes§r%nThe Telekinesis Scanner Core scans §119×19§r chunks around the player, with a radius of §19§r chunks or §1144§r blocks. Shift+right-click switches between ore-vein and underground-fluid modes.%n%n§3§lDependency and cost§r%n§cVisualProspecting is required; scanning is unavailable without it.§r Each scan requires a food level of at least §16§r and adds §124§r exhaustion. Results appear through VisualProspecting's client map integration.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nCraft §11§r Telekinesis Scanner Core to complete this quest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§2§lFollow the Map
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=§3§lMap results§r%nThe scanner sends ore-vein and underground-fluid data to VisualProspecting's client map integration, such as JourneyMap markers. The display depends on the installed and enabled integration. Coordinates are not printed line by line in chat.%n%n§3§lOperation and completion§r%nCheck that VisualProspecting and its map integration are available, then use scan markers to plan exploration. Read how results are displayed and tick the checkbox; this quest does not check a scan count.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§d§lLord of the Rings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=§3§lRings and slots§r%nWith Baubles-Expanded installed, the ring row expands to §110§r slots; without it, §12§r slots are used. Seven functional rings are rare drops from §17§r kinds of structure chest. Windrider is obtained by crafting.%n%n§3§lBundled trade sources§r%nDefault prices are §18§r Shimmering Coins each for Distant Grasp, Skywalk and Ironheart; §112§r each for Dragon's Breath, Mountainbreaker and Tempest; and §112§r Shimmering Coins plus Delighted Meals ×§116§r for Gluttony. Servers can change these trades.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the slot and ring-source information, then tick the checkbox. Later quests explain each ring's effects and retrieval requirements.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§3§lDistant Grasp
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=§3§lReach bonus§r%nEach Distant Grasp adds §12§r blocks of interaction reach and §12§r blocks of attack reach. Multiple rings stack linearly. Equipping applies the bonus and removing the ring removes it; no extra toggle is needed.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Distant Grasp for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Equip the ring to use its effect.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§c§lIronheart
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=§3§lMaximum health§r%nEach Ironheart adds §120§r maximum health, equal to §110§r hearts. Multiple rings stack linearly. Equipping and removing rings updates the health limit; it does not permanently increase base health.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Ironheart for retrieval. It is §2not consumed§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§5§lDragon's Breath
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=§3§lMaintained potion effects§r%nWhile equipped, Dragon's Breath maintains §2Fire Resistance, Night Vision, Regeneration I and Resistance I§r. Effects refresh every §15 seconds§r and last §130 seconds§r per refresh, so they remain active while the ring stays equipped and refreshes normally.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Dragon's Breath for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. These potion effects do not provide immunity to all damage.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§2§lGluttony
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=§3§lRegular and emergency feeding§r%nGluttony restores §11§r food point per second, switching to saturation when food is full. If food level is below §15§r and at least §160 seconds§r have passed since the last emergency refill, both food and saturation are filled to §120§r.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Gluttony for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Both feeding effects require the ring to be equipped.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§d§lWindrider, the Final Ring
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=§3§lRecipe and effect§r%nCraft Windrider using §11§r each of Distant Grasp, Ironheart, Dragon's Breath, Gluttony, Tempest, Mountainbreaker and Skywalk, plus Neko Coins ×§12§r. It is not one of the seven functional rings dropped in structure chests.%n%nEquipping Windrider grants §2creative flight without exhaustion cost§r.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nCraft §11§r Windrider yourself. Holding a ready-made ring does not replace the crafting check.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§2§lQuests That Unlock Trades
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=§3§lQuest gates§r%nVending-machine entries can require completion of a specified BetterQuesting quest. Unmet conditions keep an entry locked; §cthe gate allows access if BetterQuesting is absent or the query fails§r.%n%n§3§lEntry cooldowns and limits§r%nCooldowns use each player's history for each trade entry. Some bundled entries use §16 / 22 / 88 hours§r; this does not rotate a whole page's stock. Entries with unlimited uses may still have cooldowns. Check the entry display and server settings for the actual limits.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the unlocking and cooldown rules, then tick the checkbox and view the unlocked entries.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§b§lTempest
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=§3§lMovement effects§r%nWhile equipped, Tempest maintains §2Speed II and Jump Boost II§r, refreshing §130-second§r effects every §15 seconds§r. The bonuses remain active while the ring stays equipped and refreshes normally.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Tempest for retrieval. It is §2not consumed§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§6§lMountainbreaker
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=§3§lCombat and mining effects§r%nWhile equipped, Mountainbreaker maintains §2Strength II and Haste II§r, refreshing §130-second§r effects every §15 seconds§r. These improve attack strength and mining speed respectively.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Mountainbreaker for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Maintaining the bonuses requires the ring to stay equipped and refresh normally.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§9§lSkywalk
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=§3§lStep height§r%nEquipping Skywalk raises step height to §11.1§r blocks, allowing you to §2step onto a one-block rise without jumping§r. It increases step height and does not provide wall climbing.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Skywalk for retrieval. It is §2not consumed§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=§b§lTeaming Up
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=§3§lCreating and joining a team§r%nEnter /gtnhteam to open GTNHLib's team interface. Create a team, invite players or accept an invitation to join.%n%n§3§lShared wallet§r%nGTIT automatically uses the shared team wallet after you join; no separate mode needs enabling. Personal balances remain separate and are not automatically transferred. Leaving restores access to your personal wallet.%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nRead the team controls and fund-sharing rules, then tick the checkbox. Joining a team is not required by this quest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=§b§lReincarnation 101
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=§3§lPreparing for reincarnation§r%nReincarnation requires a strictly singleplayer world; §cLAN-open worlds and dedicated servers are unsupported§r. Craft a crystal with Shimmering Coins ×§14§r, Neko Coins ×§14§r and a diamond ×§11§r. Deposit the items you want to carry in the reincarnation interface, then pass the two-stage confirmation to start a new cycle. Successful reincarnation §cconsumes §11§r§c crystal from your inventory§r.%n%n§3§lNew cycle and reward delivery§r%nThe world is regenerated and progress resets, while unlocked deposit rows and columns remain. Rewards depend only on this cycle's deposits and §cdo not accumulate across cycles§r. Automatic delivery begins about §15 seconds§r after your first login in the new cycle. Each item enters your inventory near the end of its animation; only overflow drops on the ground. No manual claim is needed.%n%n§3§lThis quest's requirements§r%nTick the information checkbox and hold §11§r Reincarnation Crystal for retrieval; §cboth tasks are required§r. The quest's retrieval §2does not consume the crystal§r or require actual reincarnation. Distinguish this quest check from the crystal consumed by the reincarnation operation.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=§d§lNeko Infinity Storage Unit
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=§3§lInfinite storage across channels§r%nThe Neko Infinity Storage Unit supports items, fluids and registered third-party storage channels available at runtime. Supported types are stored separately while sharing §11§r ME drive slot.%n%n§3§lObtaining and migrating cells§r%nThe bundled trade costs §1512§r Shimmering Coins, §14§r §116,384k§r item cells and §14§r §116,384k§r fluid cells. Alternatively, shapelessly craft §11§r old infinite item cell with §11§r old infinite fluid cell into the new unit.%n%n§cEmpty the old cells through an ME-IO Port before migration. The recipe converts the cells without transferring their stored contents. Once the old cells are consumed, any contents left inside lose their access point.§r%n%n§3§lCompletion§r%nHold §11§r Neko Infinity Storage Unit for retrieval. It is §2not consumed§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=Neko Dimension Pocket
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=§3§lPortable storage and channels§r%nThe Neko Dimension Pocket provides §1135§r base storage slots, fluid and essentia management, and ME channel transfers. It can be worn. Enabled channels can keep working while carried with the GUI closed; configure and enable the relevant channels first.%n%n§3§lCrafting and upgrades§r%nThe base recipe uses a Neko Infinity Storage Unit ×§11§r, ender pearls ×§12§r, an eye of ender ×§11§r and leather ×§15§r. It accepts §15§r upgrade types: capacity, stacking, magnet, channel persistence and mage. Each upgrade costs §164§r Shimmering Coins in the bundled trades.%n%n§3§lCompletion and reward§r%nHold §11§r Neko Dimension Pocket for retrieval; it is §2not consumed§r. Choose §11§r of the §15§r upgrade types as the quest reward; all five are not granted together.
# BQ quests [pack=gtit] END

